          make no promise, warranty or guarantee that any code is valid, active, or will redeem
          successfully. Codes can expire at any time without notice — even between a source’s last
          update and the moment you try one.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Informational use only.</strong> The site is provided for general information
          about publicly listed Roblox redeem codes. It is not advice, and using it is at your own
          discretion and risk.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Unofficial and independent.</strong> rbxeyes is a fan-made tracker. It is not
          affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by Roblox Corporation or any game developer or
          publisher. Roblox and all game names, characters and trademarks belong to their
          respective owners.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Codes are free.</strong> We do not sell codes, memberships or anything else, and
          we never will. Redeem codes only through the game’s own interface; anyone asking you to
          pay for a code, log in, or share a password is not us and should not be trusted.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No warranty.</strong> The site and its content are provided “as is” and “as
          available”, without warranties of any kind. We don’t warrant the site will be
          uninterrupted, error-free, or that data (including source dates and reward wording) is
          accurate or complete — we report discrepancies openly instead of hiding them.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Limitation of liability.</strong> To the fullest extent permitted by law, we are
          not liable for any loss or damage arising from your use of, or reliance on, this site or
          its content — including codes that fail to redeem or rewards that differ from what a
          source described.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Changes.</strong> We may update the site, its content and these terms at any
          time without notice. The month in each headline and every “last read” date reflect our
          own manual read dates, not a promise of freshness.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact.</strong> Questions about these terms:{' '}
          <a href="mailto:noaitell@knowhy.net">noaitell@knowhy.net</a>.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
